{"content":{"result":[{"rank_order":1,"title":"connecting-vpcs-with-peering","skill_description":"Establishes VPC peering connections between two VPCs for direct private network connectivity. Always use this skill when creating or managing VPC peering — it validates CIDR overlap, updates all route tables in both VPCs, configures DNS resolution, and provides security group guidance that are critical for correct connectivity.\n\nServices: ec2, vpc\nTasks: configure, deploy\nPersona: developer, devops\nWorkload: networking\n*","skill_name":"connecting-vpcs-with-peering"},{"rank_order":2,"title":"configuring-vpc-endpoints-for-private-aws-service-access","skill_description":"Configures VPC endpoints (interface and gateway) for private AWS service access using AWS PrivateLink. Use when setting up secure private connectivity to S3, DynamoDB, and other AWS services without internet gateway, NAT device, or public IP addresses. Covers endpoint creation, security groups, route tables, and DNS configuration.\n\nServices: ec2, vpc, s3, dynamodb\nTasks: configure\nPersona: developer, devops\nWorkload: networking\n*","skill_name":"configuring-vpc-endpoints-for-private-aws-service-access"},{"rank_order":3,"title":"Amazon Bedrock AgentCore Runtime, Browser, and Code Interpreter add support for VPC, AWS PrivateLink, CloudFormation, and tagging - AWS","context":"Amazon Bedrock has expanded the capabilities of its AgentCore Runtime, Browser, and Code Interpreter services. These enhancements include support for Amazon Virtual Private Cloud (VPC), AWS PrivateLink, AWS CloudFormation, and resource tagging. With VPC connectivity, AgentCore services can securely access private resources within a VPC without internet exposure. AWS PrivateLink provides a private connection between a VPC and Amazon Bedrock AgentCore services. CloudFormation support enables automated resource provisioning through infrastructure as code. Resource tagging allows for cost allocation, access control, and resource organization across AgentCore deployments. AgentCore Runtime, Browser, and Code Interpreter are currently in preview and available in select AWS regions. For more information, consult the documentation on configuring VPC for AgentCore, using AWS PrivateLink with AgentCore, AgentCore CloudFormation Reference, and tagging AgentCore resources","url":"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/whats-new/2025/09/amazon-bedrock-agentcore-runtime-browser-code-interpreter-vpc-privatelink-cloudformation-tagging/"},{"rank_order":4,"title":"creating-production-vpc-multi-az","skill_description":"Creates a production-ready VPC with public and private subnets across multiple Availability Zones, including internet gateway, NAT gateways, route tables, and security groups following AWS Well-Architected principles. Use when deploying multi-AZ VPC infrastructure with automatic CIDR planning and DNS resolution.\n\nServices: ec2, vpc\nTasks: create, configure\nPersona: developer, devops\nWorkload: networking\n*","skill_name":"creating-production-vpc-multi-az"}]}}"}]}], "label": "Search AWS docs for Bedrock VPC endpoint check"}
